ol. Crystallogr.</source> <volume>53</volume> <fpage>240</fpage>-255<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15299926</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref34"><label>34</label><citation citation-type="journal">Morris, A. L., MacArthur, M. W., Hutchinson, E. G., and Thornton, J. M. (<year>1992</year>) <source>Proteins</source> <volume>12</volume> <fpage>345</fpage>-364<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1579569</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref35"><label>35</label><citation citation-type="journal">Potterton, E., McNicholas, S., Krissinel, E., Cowtan, K., and Noble, M. (<year>2002</year>) <source>Acta Crystallogr. D. Biol. Crystallogr.</source> <volume>58</volume> <fpage>1955</fpage>-1957<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12393928</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref36"><label>36</label><citation citation-type="journal">Konarev, P. V., Petoukhov, M. V., Volkov, V. V., and Svergun, D. I. (<year>2006</year>) <source>J. Appl. Crystallogr.</source> <volume>39</volume> <fpage>277</fpage>-286</citation></ref><ref id="ref37"><label>37</label><citation citation-type="journal">Svergun, D. I., Petoukhov, M. V., and Koch, M. H. (<year>2001</year>) <source>Biophys. J.</source> <volume>80</volume> <fpage>2946</fpage>-2953<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11371467</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref38"><label>38</label><citation citation-type="journal">Lim, C. J., Han, J., Yousefi, N., Ma, Y., Amieux, P. S., McKnight, G. S., Taylor, S. S., and Ginsberg, M. H. (<year>2007</year>) <source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>9</volume> <fpage>415</fpage>-421<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17369818</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref39"><label>39</label><citation citation-type="journal">Xu, W., Baribault, H., and Adamson, E. D. (<year>1998</year>) <source>Development</source> <volume>125</volume> <fpage>327</fpage>-337<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9486805</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref40"><label>40</label><citation citation-type="journal">van der Ven, P. F., Wiesner, S., Salmikangas, P., Auerbach, D., Himmel, M., Kempa, S., Hayess, K., Pacholsky, D., Taivainen, A., Schroder, R., Carpen, O., and Furst, D. O. (<year>2000</year>) <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>151</volume> <fpage>235</fpage>-248<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11038172</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref41"><label>41</label><citation citation-type="journal">Holm, L., and Sander, C. (<year>1995</year>) <source>Trends Biochem. Sci.</source> <volume>20</volume> <fpage>478</fpage>-480<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8578593</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref42"><label>42</label><citation citation-type="journal">Patel, B., Gingras, A. R., Bobkov, A. A., Fujimoto, L. M., Zhang, M., Liddington, R. C., Mazzeo, D., Emsley, J., Roberts, G. C., Barsukov, I. L., and Critchley, D. R. (<year>2006</year>) <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>281</volume> <fpage>7458</fpage>-7467<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16407302</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref43"><label>43</label><citation citation-type="journal">Gilmore, A. P., Wood, C., Ohanian, V., Jackson, P., Patel, B., Rees, D. J., Hynes, R. O., and Critchley, D. R. (<year>1993</year>) <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>122</volume> <fpage>337</fpage>-347<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8320257</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref44"><label>44</label><citation citation-type="journal">Rodius, S., Chaloin, O., Moes, M., Schaffner-Reckinger, E., Landrieu, I., Lippens, G., Lin, M., Zhang, J., and Kieffer, N. (<year>2008</year>) <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>283</volume> <fpage>24212</fpage>-24223<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18577523</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref45"><label>45</label><citation citation-type="journal">Goksoy, E., Ma, Y. Q., Wang, X., Kong, X., Perera, D., Plow, E. F., and Qin, J. (<year>2008</year>) <source>Mol. Cell</source> <volume>31</volume> <fpage>124</fpage>-133<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18614051</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="fn4"><label>2</label><p>The abbreviations used are: IBS2, integrin-binding site 2; GST, glutathione <italic>S</italic>-transferase; SeMet, selenomethionine; SAXS, small angle x-ray scattering; ELISA, enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay; PBS, phosphate-buffered saline; GFP, green fluorescent protein; DSC, differential scanning calorimetry; r.m.s.d., root mean square deviation; Vd1, vinculin d1 domain; FA, focal adhesion; Fmoc, 9-fluorenylmethyloxycarbonyl.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>